{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"debug":1},true],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"zotero":1,"inscriptions":7,"isBulletin":145},{"title":2,"author":3,"date":4,"citation":5,"uri":6},"L'Agorà (scavi 1970-2004)","Scibona","2009","\u003Cspan>G. Scibona, «L’Agorà (scavi 1970-2004)», in \u003Ci>Alaisa-Halaesa. Scavi e ricerche (1970-2007)\u003C/i>, a c. di G. Scibona e G. Tigano (Messina: Regione Siciliana, 2009), 9–43\u003C/span>","https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/DSZEF4K5",[8],{"file":9,"uri":9,"title":10,"status":11,"editions":13,"editionAuthor":25,"type":26,"objectType":30,"material":34,"condition":49,"layoutDesc":50,"handNote":57,"date":74,"places":79,"geo":90,"country":84,"provenance":81,"provenanceGeo":94,"region":95,"settlement":81,"repository":96,"idno":100,"textLang":103,"tmNumber":15,"facsimile":107,"letterHeights":114,"publications":118,"zotero":122,"keywords":126,"html":137,"bibl":138,"bulletinDateSort":144,"citedRangeSort":139,"languageSort":104,"materialSort":35,"typeSort":27},"ISic003591","Honours for Aelius Asinius Petitus, rhetor",{"_":12},"edited",[14,17,19,21,23],{"_":15,"type":16},"645670","TM",{"type":18},"EDR",{"type":20},"EDH",{"type":22},"EDCS",{"type":24},"PHI",null,{"_":27,"ana":28,"ref":29},"honorific","#function.honorific","https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Honorific",{"_":31,"ana":32,"ref":33},"plaque","#object.plaque","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259",{"_":35,"ana":36,"type":37,"subtype":38,"resp":40,"ref":41,"placeName":42},"Very fine to fine-grained, banded, grey, calcitic, smelly marble, likely Lunense. Optical microscopy: homeoblastic fabric with triple points, lineated. Digital microscopy: heteroblastic to homeoblastic fabric (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy, XRD, optical microscopy, stable isotopes analysis)\n","#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Lunense","stone.marble",[39],"Lunense","#Coccato","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html",{"type":43,"ref":44,"location":47},"provenance",{"_":45,"target":46},"Carrara","https://www.geonames.org/6542087/carrara.html",{"geo":48},"44.06294,10.06069","",{"layout":51},{"p":52,"rs":53,"damage":49},"Five lines of Greek letters are preserved.",{"_":54,"ana":55,"ref":56},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"lettering":58,"dimensions":59},"The letters are very neatly and regularly V-cut, well spaced and generously proportioned; height 56-63 mm. Serifs are mostly deep triangular terminations to the principal strokes. Σ and Ε are lunate, the latter with a short middle bar; Ν has a rounded join between the second and third strokes; Α has a slight apex, and a horizontal bar; Π has vertical hastae of equal length, and the cross-bar overlaps slightly on both sides; Ρ is not quite closed, with a well-rounded eye; the vertical stroke of Φ extends up to join the base of the letter on the line above. Interpuncts are used regularly to mark word-breaks and have the form of a comma.",[60,69],{"type":61,"l":62,"from":63,"to":64,"h":65,"unit":66,"atLeast":67,"atMost":68},"letterHeight","Lines 1-5","line1","line5","56-63","mm","56","63",{"type":70,"l":71,"from":63,"to":72,"h":73,"unit":66},"interlinear","Interlineation","line2","not measured",{"_":75,"notBefore":76,"notAfter":77,"evidence":78},"Second half of 2nd century CE",151,200,"context",[80,85],{"_":81,"type":82,"ref":83,"region":84},"Halaesa","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462225","Sicilia",{"_":86,"type":87,"ref":88,"offset":89,"region":84},"Castel di Tusa","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/2525099","near",[91],[92,93],37.99907,14.26197,[],"Sicily",{"_":97,"role":98,"ref":99},"Antiquarium e sito archeologico di Halaesa ","museum","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/053",{"_":101,"type":102},"30602","inventory",{"_":104,"mainLang":105,"languages":106},"Ancient Greek","grc",[104],{"n":108,"url":109,"height":110,"width":111,"desc":112,